## Transport (single adapter)

Each endpoint uses either **Chat Completions** (`POST {base_url}/chat/completions`) or the **Responses API** (`POST {base_url}/responses`), selected by `LLMConfig.api_protocol` (`chat` default). Images go in as base64 `image_url` content blocks (Chat) or `input_image` items inside a `type: message` wrapper (Responses). Text-only Responses turns use plain-string `content` (or `input` as a lone string for a single user turn); assistant replay never uses `input_text` blocks. `base_url` is the API root (e.g. `https://api.openai.com/v1`, `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`, `https://api.poe.com/v1`, `http://localhost:11434/v1`). Local servers stay on Chat Completions with reasoning off; OpenRouter GPT-5.5 can use Chat + `reasoning`; Poe reasoning models should use Responses. **Claude models** (`claude` in `model_name`): reasoning effort maps to `thinking: {type: adaptive}` + `output_config: {effort}` (not top-level `reasoning`, which Poe translates to deprecated `thinking.type.enabled` on 4.6+). Reasoning summary `auto` adds `thinking.display: summarized`.

**Reasoning**: `LLMConfig.reasoning_effort` / `reasoning_summary` / `reasoning_max_tokens` control per-endpoint thinking. Blank effort/summary ⇒ inherit `LLM_REASONING_EFFORT_DEFAULT` / `LLM_REASONING_SUMMARY_DEFAULT` from System Settings (defaults `off` / `auto`). Endpoint `off` always omits reasoning params. `_resolve_reasoning(config)` builds the provider `reasoning` object; `_merge_request_extra` shallow-merges validated `request_extra_json` (provider-specific keys, e.g. Poe Chat `extra_body` fields). Batch AI Tools get reasoning automatically via `chat()` / `chat_messages()`; saved assets use **final answer text only** — `info['reasoning']` is diagnostics/UI, never written to ANS/SOL/MD.

**Service tier**: `LLMConfig.service_tier` / `service_tier_batch` (blank/`flex`/`priority`/`auto`/`default`) are added to Chat Completions bodies as the top-level `service_tier` param **only when non-empty**. Batch SSE ops set transient `config._batch = True` to opt into `service_tier_batch`. Set per-endpoint in `templates/admin_llm_endpoints.html` (`#epServiceTier` / `#epServiceTierBatch`).

- `llm_client.chat(config, system, user_text, images)` → `(text, info)` where `info = {usage, finish_reason, reasoning, reasoning_details, raw}`; raises `LLMError`. Dispatches by `api_protocol`. `_extract_message_parts` / `_extract_responses_parts` separate answer text from reasoning.
- `llm_client.chat_messages(config, messages, max_tokens?, temperature?, timeout?)` → `(text, info)` for **multi-turn** conversations. Used by batch AI Tools when not using `chat()`.
- `llm_client.chat_messages_stream(config, messages, ...)` → **generator** yielding `{type:'delta', content, reasoning}` then `{type:'done', text, reasoning, finish_reason, usage}`. Streams Chat Completions SSE or Responses semantic events. Used by **Explain** and admin **Chat** console. Interactive routes pass `LLM_CHAT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (default 600 s).
- `llm_client.prepare_image(abs_path, max_dim)` → downscaled JPEG `(b64, mime)` for sending.
- `llm_client.prepare_image_from_pil(im, max_dim)` → same, from an in-memory PIL Image (used when MD/DOC slots are rendered to pages on the fly for proofreading).
- `llm_client.read_image_data_uri(abs_path)` → ORIGINAL bytes data-URI (whole-image figure fallback).
- `llm_client.crop_image_data_uri(abs_path, box, pad, max_dim)` → PNG data-URI of a cropped region; `box` is `[x1,y1,x2,y2]` **fractions** 0..1 (top-left origin). Flattens alpha to white; raises `ValueError` for a degenerate box.
- `resolve_api_key(config)`: decrypt `api_key_enc` (Fernet) → else `os.getenv(api_key_env or 'LLM_API_KEY')`.

## API-key storage (hybrid)

Per-endpoint key entered in the UI is stored **Fernet-encrypted** in `LLMConfig.api_key_enc`; blank ⇒ fall back to `.env`. The Fernet key derives from `LLM_KEY_SECRET` (else `SECRET_KEY`) via SHA-256 → urlsafe-b64. **Rotating that secret invalidates stored ciphertexts** (re-enter keys). Plaintext keys are NEVER serialised to the browser — the data route reports only `has_stored_key` / `key_resolves`.

## SSE contract

Routes mirror `batch_generate_images`: gather work in request context, stream inside a pushed `app.app_context()`. Both ops are GET (EventSource) + `text/event-stream`.

- `GET /admin/questions/ai/check` — params `question_ids`, `endpoint_id`, `typed_version`, `ref_version`, `atypes` (csv QUE/ANS/SOL), `formats` (csv IMG/MD/DOC; `DOCX`→`DOC`, default all three), `recheck` (1/0), `parallel` (1/0; cloud only).
- `GET /admin/questions/ai/generate-md` — params `question_ids`, `endpoint_id`, `source_version`, `target_version`, `atypes`, `overwrite` (1/0), `embed_image` (1/0), `parallel` (1/0; cloud only).
- `GET /admin/questions/ai/solve-generate` — params `question_ids`, `endpoint_id`, `versions` (csv EN/CH/BI/ENO/CHO), `targets` (`ANS,SOL,ANS_TEXT`), `include_official_sol` (1/0), `overwrite` (1/0), `parallel` (1/0; cloud only). Writes ANS/SOL Markdown assets and/or version-independent `Question.answer`.
- `GET /admin/questions/ai/solve-check` — params `question_ids`, `endpoint_id`, `versions`, `targets` (`ANS,SOL,ANS_TEXT`), `formats` (IMG/MD/DOC for asset targets), `include_official_sol`, `parallel`. Writes `QuestionAsset.check_state/check_result/checked_at` for ANS/SOL asset formats; ANS_TEXT checks are log-only and do not persist state.
- `POST /admin/questions/ai/cancel` — body `{job_id}`.
- `GET /admin/questions/ai/endpoints` — enabled endpoints for the modal dropdown (subject-admin OK).
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/ai/generate-md` — **synchronous** (not SSE) per-slot MD generation for the edit-modal button; body `{version, asset_type, endpoint_id, embed_image?, overwrite?, source_version?}` (`source_version` defaults to `version`; UI shows the button when any version has IMG for that atype and offers a source-version picker); returns `{success, status, message, asset_id}`.
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/ai/check` — **synchronous** per-slot proofread for the edit-modal Quick-Check button; body `{version, asset_type, ref_version, endpoint_id, recheck?, formats?}`; calls `check_slot` (all present formats by default) → `{success, status, state, message}` (status ∈ ok|issues|skip|error).
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/ai/solve-generate` — sync ANS/SOL Markdown generation from QUE; body `{version, asset_type: ANS|SOL, endpoint_id?, include_official_sol?, overwrite?}`.
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/ai/solve-check` — sync ANS/SOL solve-check; body `{version, asset_type: ANS|SOL, endpoint_id?, include_official_sol?, formats?}`.
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/ai/answer-text` — sync Answer Text solve op; body `{mode: "generate"|"check", source_versions[], endpoint_id?, include_official_sol?, overwrite?}`. Generate writes `Question.answer`; check returns findings only.
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/generate-img` — **synchronous** render of ONE slot's MD/DOC source into IMG part(s) for the edit-modal Gen-IMG button; body `{version, asset_type, source_format?, stitch?}` (`source_format` ∈ DOC|MD|'' auto). Reuses `batch_image_gen` (Word COM) + `replace_img_assets`. Returns `{success, message, wrote, deleted, source_format}`.
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/check-state` — **manual** set/clear of a slot's proofread status; body `{version, asset_type, state, note?, severity?}` where `state ∈ ok|issues|error|clear`. Writes check fields to ALL rows in the slot; `clear` nulls them. Manual edits store `checked_by: "manual"` + `editor` username. Drives the editable status bar.
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/ai/suggest-tags` — **synchronous**, no DB write. Body `{versions[], fields[], endpoint_id?}` → returns `{suggestions, display_names, unmatched[], raw}` for the edit modal to populate + highlight (user clicks Save Tags to commit).
- `GET /admin/questions/ai/auto-tag` — SSE batch tagging. Params `question_ids, endpoint_id, versions, fields, overwrite, parallel` (1/0; cloud only) → `iter_auto_tag` (suggest + apply + commit per question). Reuses `/admin/questions/ai/cancel`.
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/verify` — set the whole-question `verified` flag; body `{verified}`; response includes `unchecked_assets` so the modal can soft-warn.
- `POST /admin/questions/batch-set-verified` — body `{question_ids[], verified}` (subject-scoped).
- `POST /admin/questions/batch-set-check-state` — body `{question_ids[], versions[], atypes[], state, note?, severity?, overwrite?}`; applies the per-slot check write across the selection (skips empty slots; `overwrite=false` skips slots already carrying a status).

Event dicts: `{type, message, current?, total?, ...}`. `type` ∈ `job` (first; carries `job_id`) / `info` / `skip` / `success` / `error` / `done`. The `done` event carries `stats` (`{ok, issues, skipped, errors}` for check/solve-check; `{created, skipped, errors}` for MD; `{created, updated, skipped, errors}` for solve-generate).

## Per-feature default LLM endpoints

Every AI feature has its own `*_DEFAULT_LLM` System Setting (string = endpoint name, blank = auto-pick). Resolution is centralised in `app/llm_client.resolve_default_endpoint(setting_key, vision_only=True, named_vision_only=None)`:

1. If `current_app.config[setting_key]` names an enabled endpoint (and is vision-capable when `named_vision_only`), use it.
2. Else first enabled endpoint by `sort_order, name` (filtered to vision-capable when `vision_only`).
3. Else `None`.

| Setting | Resolver | `endpoint_id` request param required? |
|---|---|---|
| `EXPLAIN_DEFAULT_LLM` | `_default_explain_endpoint` (`named_vision_only=False`) | optional admin override |
| `AUTOTAG_DEFAULT_LLM` | `_default_ai_endpoint('AUTOTAG_DEFAULT_LLM')` | optional (server falls back) |
| `MD_DEFAULT_LLM` | `_default_ai_endpoint('MD_DEFAULT_LLM')` | optional |
| `CHECK_DEFAULT_LLM` | `_default_ai_endpoint('CHECK_DEFAULT_LLM')` | optional |
| `SOLVEGEN_DEFAULT_LLM` | `_default_ai_endpoint('SOLVEGEN_DEFAULT_LLM')` | optional |
| `SOLVECHECK_DEFAULT_LLM` | `_default_ai_endpoint('SOLVECHECK_DEFAULT_LLM')` | optional |
| `PDF_IMPORT_DEFAULT_LLM` | `_pdf_default_endpoint` (then falls through to `EXPLAIN_DEFAULT_LLM`) | optional |

Server-side validation goes through `_ai_load_endpoint(default_setting_key)` (query) / `_ai_load_endpoint_from_body(data, default_setting_key)` (JSON body) — both return `(cfg, error_response, status)` and fall back to the per-feature default when `endpoint_id` is missing/blank/`0`.

Client-side: `GET /admin/questions/ai/endpoints` returns `{endpoints: [...], defaults: {tag, md, check, solvegen, solvecheck}}`. Edit-modal helpers use `_aiPickDefaultEndpointId(eps, defaults, opKey)` (in `templates/partials/edit_question_modal_js.html`) to pick the right id; the AI Tools modal in `admin_questions.html` re-applies the default whenever the op radio changes (`aiToolsToggleOp` → `_aiApplyDefaultEndpoint`). PDF Import pre-selects server-side (`default_endpoint_id` template var on the `<option selected>`).

## Cancellation (real server-side Stop)

`app/ai_tools._AI_CANCEL: {job_id: threading.Event}`. Each generator checks the flag **between questions** and emits a final `done`. The frontend Stop posts the `job_id` (captured from the `job` event) and keeps the stream open so the final `done` arrives. Single-process assumption (same caveat as the settings hot-reload): the cancel POST must reach the worker running the stream.

## Parallel batch ops (local vs cloud)

Each `LLMConfig` carries `kind` (`'local'` | `'cloud'`) + `max_concurrency` (int, default 1). The SSE batch generators — `iter_check`, `iter_generate_md`, `iter_solve_generate`, `iter_solve_check`, `iter_auto_tag` (this file) and `iter_detect` ([app/pdf_import.py](mdc:app/pdf_import.py)) — take `parallel`, `app`, `max_workers` kwargs and **fan their per-item LLM round-trips across a thread pool only when the endpoint is cloud AND the route passed `parallel=1`**; otherwise they run the unchanged sequential loop. Local endpoints are always sequential.

- **Executor**: `app/parallel.run_parallel(app, cancel, items, worker_fn, max_workers)` — generator yielding `{item, result, error}` in **completion order**; each worker runs inside `app.app_context()` (Flask-SQLAlchemy gives a thread-local scoped session). `max_workers<=1` ⇒ sequential fallback. A cancelled-before-start worker returns the `CANCELLED` sentinel (consumer skips it, no counter/event). In-flight requests finish naturally — same cancel semantics as the sequential loops.
- **Per-item units**: `generate_md_slot` / `check_slot` / `solve_generate_slot` / `generate_answer_text` / `solve_check_slot_format` / `check_answer_text` / `_auto_tag_one` / `detect_page` — pure functions returning a result dict (or raising, which the consumer turns into an `error` event). **All counter updates + event shaping happen on the consumer thread**, never in workers.
- **Word COM**: in parallel `iter_check`, each worker owns a **short-lived `_LazyWord`** (opened + closed inside the worker) so MD/DOC pre-rendering still serialises on the global `word_com._WORD_COM_LOCK` while pure-IMG checks run fully concurrently. The sequential path keeps the single reused session.
- **PDF detect ordering**: in parallel `iter_detect`, custom-prompt (`generic_prompt`) auto-numbering is assigned **once at the end** in reading order `(page, box top-Y)` per side (`_number_custom`) so question numbers are deterministic regardless of completion order.
- **Routes**: `_ai_parallel(cfg, want_parallel)` (in [app/admin.py](mdc:app/admin.py)) returns `(on, workers)` — `on` only when `want_parallel and cfg.kind=='cloud' and max_concurrency>1`. The PDF detect route inlines the same gate.
- **Migration**: `app/__init__.py` adds the two columns idempotently on start-up and back-fills `kind='cloud', max_concurrency=4` for known hosted API hosts (OpenAI / OpenRouter / Google / Anthropic / Groq / Together / DeepSeek / Mistral / xAI).
- **UI**: a **Run in parallel** checkbox (auto-shown only for cloud endpoints, default checked) sits by the endpoint pickers in `templates/admin_questions.html` (`aiUpdateParallelUI`) and `templates/admin_pdf_import.html` (`updateParallelUI`); both append `&parallel=1`. Per-endpoint `kind` + `max_concurrency` are edited in `templates/admin_llm_endpoints.html` (`#epKind` / `#epMaxConcurrency`, `onKindChange` pins local→1).

## Check-state semantics

`check_slot_format(question, atype, typed_version, ref_version, file_format, ...)` is the **atomic worker** (one IMG / MD / DOC check). `check_slot` runs every present format in `formats` (default IMG+MD+DOC) and aggregates. `iter_check` loops `(question, atype, format)` work items (SSE). `ai_check_slot` calls `check_slot` once for Quick Check.

- **Image resolution** — typed side: `_resolve_format_images` (IMG parts as-is; MD/DOC rendered via `_render_source_to_pages`). Reference side: `_resolve_slot_images` (IMG preferred, else rendered DOC/MD).
- **Lazy Word session (`_LazyWord`)** — `iter_check` opens ONE Word COM session for the whole run (sequential path), but only when a work item needs rendering. Pure-IMG checks never acquire the Word lock. Parallel workers each own a short-lived session.
- **Write target** — `_write_format_check_state` writes `check_state`/`check_result`/`checked_at` to every row of **that format only** in the typed slot. `check_result` includes `file_format`.
- Skips (with event) if typed/reference slot has no usable source, or if already checked and `recheck` is off. Sends reference images first, then typed; parses strict JSON via `ai_prompts.parse_check_result`. States: `ok` (faithful), `issues` (discrepancies listed), `error` (unparseable reply — raw stored). `check_result` JSON: `{status, issues:[{severity,location,description}], model, ref_version, checked_by}` (manual edits use `checked_by:"manual"` + `editor`).

**Status rollup is typed-only.** In `questions_api_list`, the per-question **Status** indicator + `check_status` filter consider only `TYPED_VERSIONS` (EN/CH/BI, from `app/utils.py`); `OFFICIAL_VERSIONS` (ENO/CHO) are the reference scans and are excluded. `asset_count` still reflects the true total across all versions.

The edit-modal slot header keeps a compact badge (`renderCheckBadge`, now reads ALL slot parts), and the section shows a prominent **editable** status bar (`renderCheckStatusBar`, shown whenever the slot has ANY asset — IMG/MD/DOC, even unchecked): colour-coded OK/issues/error/"Not proofread", the issue list, and inline buttons — **AI proofread** (`openQuickCheckModal` → `runQuickCheck` → `ai_check_slot`), **mark correct / mark issue… / clear** (`setSlotCheckState` → `set_asset_check_state`). MD and DOC cards also get a **Gen IMG** button (`genImgButtonHtml` → `generateImgFromSlot` → `generate_img_slot`). All gated on `window.OQB_AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` (admin + dashboard).

## Edit-modal Prev/Next navigation

The edit modal header has Prev/Next arrows + an "n / total" counter (`#editNavControls`). `openEditModal(questionId, {preserveView})` keeps the active main tab + version pill when navigating; `oqbEditNavGo(±1)` steps through `window.oqbEditNav.ids`. The ordered ID list is read fresh on each open from a host-provided `window.oqbEditNavSource()` — **dashboard** returns the full filtered set (`#allQuestionIds` across all pages), **admin** returns the current page's `#questionTableBody tr.q-row` data-ids.

## Auto-tagging semantics

Classify a question with a vision LLM and map returned **names** back to the subject's Topic/Subtopic/Chapter/Subchapter IDs.

- **Inputs** (`_resolve_tag_inputs`): for QUE then SOL, across the requested versions in order, take the FIRST available content per type — **IMG parts** (`prepare_image`) → else the **MD text** (data-URIs stripped to keep the prompt small) → else a **DOC slot rendered to a PNG** via `doc_thumbnails.ensure_thumbnail` (polled briefly). QUE is required; SOL optional.
- **Prompt**: `TAG_SYSTEM` (role + STRICT JSON contract) + `TAG_USER` (vars `subject_name`, `fields`, `taxonomy`). `build_tag_taxonomy(subject_id, fields)` renders only the requested fields' allowed values (Topics→Subtopics, Chapters→Subchapters, q_type/level enums). The model must choose ONLY from these names.
- **Parse + map** (`parse_tag_result` → `_map_tag_names`): defensive JSON extraction (fenced/bare); names matched case-insensitively within the subject. Subtopics validated as children of their resolved topic; `major_subtopic` must belong to `major_topic`. Topics/Subtopics share one list each (major + minor). Unmatched names are reported, not invented.
- **`suggest_tags`** returns suggestions + display names + unmatched (NO write) — used by the sync route for review-before-save. **`apply_tags`** writes only the requested fields, skipping any field already holding a value when `overwrite` is off (scalar + M2M lists). **`iter_auto_tag`** is the SSE batch generator (job/info/skip/success/error/done + cancel between questions), calling `suggest_tags`+`apply_tags` and committing per question.
- Field keys: `q_type` (MC/CQ), `level` (1-3), `section`, `major_topic`, `major_subtopic`, `minor_topics[]`, `subtopics[]`, `chapter`, `subchapter`. Defaults the UI pre-selects: `q_type, major_topic, major_subtopic, chapter`.

## MD generation

`generate_md_slot(question, atype, source_version, target_version, ...)` is the **shared single-slot worker** (returns `{status: created|updated|skip|error, message, asset_id?}`). `iter_generate_md` loops it per slot and maps results to SSE events; the synchronous `ai_generate_md_slot` route calls it once.

Per slot: load source IMG parts → `MD_SYSTEM` LLM call → `strip_md_fences` → `normalize_inline_math` (tightens `$ x $` → `$x$` so pandoc/docx renders it — `tex_math_dollars` rejects spaced inline delimiters; the prompt also asks for tight `$x$`). **Figures are only embedded when the transcription actually contains a `[FIGURE: ...]` placeholder** (`ai_prompts.FIGURE_RE` / `figure_captions`) — pure-text questions yield Markdown only, no image. When figures exist and `embed_image` is on, `_embed_figures` runs a **second LLM "locate figures" pass** (`build_figure_box_system()` → `parse_figure_boxes` with 0–1000 grid + `PDF_IMPORT_COORD_ORDER`) for single-image slots and replaces each placeholder with a **cropped** base64 image (`crop_image_data_uri`); it falls back to the **whole** source image when the box is missing/degenerate/near-full-page (`_box_is_useful`) or the slot has multiple parts. Skips+logs if the result exceeds `MD_MAX_SIZE_BYTES`. Writes to the canonical MD path (`_md_rel_path`, mirrors `admin.create_md_asset`), upserts the target `QuestionAsset`, and calls `md_render.invalidate(asset.id)`.

The prompt is strict that `[FIGURE]` is ONLY for real diagrams/graphs/drawings — never plain text, equations, tables, or MC options. Default `MD_SYSTEM` also requires escaped question numbers (`8\.`) and each MC option on its own line (GFM newline rules).

## Solve generation/checking

Solve ops are distinct from MD transcription and visual proofreading: the model is asked to work out the QUE itself.

- **Inputs**: `_solve_gather_inputs` takes QUE content from the target version, preferring IMG parts, then MD text, then rendered DOC. If `include_official_sol` is true, ENO/CHO SOL content is appended when available. Answer Text is version-independent and uses the first selected version with usable QUE content.
- **Generation**: `solve_generate_slot(question, kind, version, ...)` writes ANS/SOL Markdown assets using the same canonical `_md_rel_path` / `QuestionAsset(file_format='MD')` path and invalidates `md_render`. `generate_answer_text` writes plaintext to `Question.answer`.
- **Checking**: `solve_check_slot_format` checks each existing ANS/SOL format separately and writes `check_state/check_result/checked_at` with `mode: "solve"` in `check_result`. `check_answer_text` returns `ok/issues/skip/error` only; it intentionally does not persist any check state because `Question.answer` has no check columns.
- **Prompts**: `SOLVE_GEN_SYSTEM/USER` and `SOLVE_CHECK_SYSTEM/USER` live in the prompt registry. Solve-check reuses `parse_check_result`'s strict JSON shape so the existing status badge/bar can display issues.

## Explain (AI tutor chat — dashboard, all users)

`POST /dashboard/api/question/<id>/explain` (login-required, gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED`, subject-access checked via `has_subject_access`) drives the dashboard **Explain** button. Unlike the admin AI Tools, it's available to **any** logged-in user with access to the subject, and uses the **default endpoint** — `_default_explain_endpoint()` first honours the `EXPLAIN_DEFAULT_LLM` system setting (an endpoint name picked from a dropdown of enabled endpoints), and falls back to the first enabled, vision-capable `LLMConfig` by `sort_order,name` when the setting is blank or names a missing/disabled endpoint.

- Body `{turns: [{role, content, images?}], version_priority?, endpoint_id?}`. `turns` is the conversation AFTER the (server-built) initial image turn; empty for the first request. Stateless: the server rebuilds turn 1 (system `EXPLAIN_SYSTEM` + labelled QUE/SOL context) every call and appends `turns`, so the **source** images aren't re-uploaded from the browser.
- **`endpoint_id` (admin-only override).** Super-admins or subject-admins of the question's subject can pass an `endpoint_id` to swap models on the fly without touching `EXPLAIN_DEFAULT_LLM`. Permission is re-checked server-side via `_can_pick_explain_endpoint(question)`; regular users' `endpoint_id` is silently ignored. The companion route `GET /dashboard/api/question/<id>/explain/endpoints` returns `{can_pick, default_id, endpoints: [{id, name, model, supports_vision}]}` — empty list for non-pickers — and is fetched on modal open to populate the dropdown. **Picker change auto-regenerates** via `_explainRegenerate()`: aborts the in-flight stream through an `AbortController` stashed on `explainState.aborter`, drops the last assistant turn from `explainState.turns` and any trailing assistant bubble(s) from the DOM, then re-fires `_explainSend(null, null)` with the same conversation history. The `onDone` and `.finally` callbacks of every stream are guarded by an `aborter`-equality check so a stale stream that lost its turn (raced with a regenerate) doesn't clobber the new stream's busy state or push a phantom assistant turn.
- **User-attached images.** Each user turn may carry an `images: [data:image/...;base64,...]` array (paste, drag-drop, or file-pick — up to 6 per turn, 8 MB each, 32 MB total per request). The server runs every URL through `llm_client.prepare_image_from_data_url` (long edge → `LLM_IMAGE_MAX_DIM`, JPEG re-encoded q=88 — same pipeline as `prepare_image` but from a data URL instead of a file path) and folds the resulting blocks into the user message as multi-modal content. The same images stay in `explainState.turns[i].images` on the client and are re-sent on every follow-up turn so the model retains visual context across the conversation. A user turn carrying images while the picked endpoint is **not** vision-capable → `400 "The selected LLM endpoint can't see images"`. Backend caps live in `app/dashboard.py` as `EXPLAIN_MAX_IMAGES_PER_TURN` / `EXPLAIN_MAX_IMAGES_TOTAL_BYTES`; frontend caps in `EXPLAIN_MAX_IMAGES_PER_TURN` / `EXPLAIN_MAX_IMAGE_BYTES` / `EXPLAIN_MAX_TOTAL_IMAGE_BYTES` constants in `templates/dashboard.html`.
- `_explain_slot_context(qid, atype, vp, ...)` prefers IMG (vision) via `_resolve_preview_assets(..., force_format='IMG')`; falls back to the slot's MD **text** when no image exists. QUE is required (image or MD); SOL is optional.
- **Response is `text/event-stream`** (SSE). Events: `{type:'preamble'}` (sent immediately so proxies see bytes) → zero-or-more `{type:'delta', content?, reasoning?}` (live tokens) → either `{type:'done', reply, reply_html, model, endpoint, has_solution}` or `{type:'error', message}`. `reply_html` is `md_render.render_text(normalize_inline_math(reply))` (sanitised; KaTeX client-side). Response headers set `X-Accel-Buffering: no` (nginx flush) and `Cache-Control: no-cache`. `chat_messages_stream` sets `resp.encoding = 'utf-8'` before iterating because LM Studio and several Ollama builds omit `charset=utf-8` and `requests` would otherwise fall back to ISO-8859-1 → mojibake on curly quotes / CJK / emoji.
- Frontend lives in `templates/dashboard.html` (`_explainStreamRequest`, `openExplainModal`, `sendExplainMessage`, plus the staging helpers `_explainStageFiles` / `_explainRenderStaged` / `_explainSyncVisionFromPicker` / `_explainApplyEndpoints`): reads `response.body.getReader()`, parses SSE blocks, accumulates content + reasoning, renders both live (reasoning in a `<details>` disclosure, content via `window.oqbRenderMarkdownLiveSplit` which throttles render to ~10 fps, freezes the rendered HTML for the stable prefix, and re-renders only the tail through `marked` + KaTeX), then on `done` swaps the bubble to the server-rendered (bleach-sanitised) Markdown HTML and runs `oqbTypesetMath`. Raw `reply` is stored in `turns` for the next request; user-attached `images` (data URLs) are stored alongside and re-sent on every follow-up turn. `partials/question_list.html` passes QUE/ANS/SOL availability flags into `openExplainModal`, which renders compact preview buttons that call the shared `previewAsset()` modal; `previewAsset()` uses a stacked z-index helper so it appears above the still-open Explain modal.

## Direct chat (super-admin endpoint console)

`POST /admin/llm-endpoints/<id>/chat` is a **raw** chat console on the LLM Endpoints management page (super-admin only). Body `{turns: [{role, content, images?}, ...]}` is passed straight to `llm_client.chat_messages_stream(cfg, messages)` with **no system prompt, no injected context, and no other guardrails** — useful for probing model behaviour, debugging Markdown formatting, or sanity-checking a newly added endpoint before exposing it via the AI Tools / Explain flows.

Same SSE contract as Explain (`preamble`/`delta`/`done`/`error`); the reply is `normalize_inline_math`'d and Markdown-rendered server-side at end-of-stream so KaTeX in the chat bubbles works the same way as the dashboard. Disabled endpoints are rejected with a 400. User turns can include pasted/dragged/file-picked `images` for endpoints with `supports_vision`; the server runs every data URL through `llm_client.prepare_image_from_data_url` (same 6 images/turn, 8 MB/image frontend, 32 MB/request server budget as Explain) and rejects images for text-only endpoints. The server caps text at 16 KiB/message and the running transcript at the most recent 40 turns. UI lives in `templates/admin_llm_endpoints.html` (`#chatModal`, `openChatModal`, `sendChatMessage`, `_chatStageFiles`, `_chatRenderStaged`) and mirrors the Explain modal's staged thumbnails, user-image bubbles, full-size overlay, streaming Markdown, and reasoning disclosure.

## Gotchas / invariants

1. Whole feature gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED`; image ops require `supports_vision`.
2. Subject-admins may run on their own subjects only — `question_ids` is intersected with `get_user_admin_subjects()` (same as the batch ops). Endpoint CRUD is super-admin only.
3. LLM JSON is unreliable — `parse_check_result` extracts fenced/bare JSON defensively and returns `None` on total failure (caller stores raw + `check_state='error'`).
4. Images are downscaled to `LLM_IMAGE_MAX_DIM` (long edge) before sending; embedded MD figures use the original bytes.
5. The dev server must run threaded for the long SSE streams (already the case for the other batch ops).
